Package: replayr
Title: Read Emulator Movie Files into a Uniform Frame-by-Frame Array
Version: 0.3.3
Authors@R: 
    person("Thorben", "Pelzer", , "thorben@pelzer.blog",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Decoders for twelve emulator movie ("input log") file
    formats used by the speedrun and tool-assisted-speedrun
    communities: 'FCEUX' (.fm2), 'BizHawk' (.bk2), 'FCEU' (.fcm),
    'lsnes' (.lsmv), 'Gens-rerecording' (.gmv), 'VBA-rerecording'
    (.vbm), 'Mupen64' (.m64), 'Snes9x-rerecording' (.smv),
    'PCSX-rerecording' (.pxm), 'PSXjin' (.pjm), 'Dolphin' (.dtm),
    and 'Doom' (.lmp). Every
    parser produces the same in-memory shape: a per-frame logical
    matrix indexed against a single 40-slot universal-button layout,
    plus the file's header metadata and a per-frame commands vector.
    Allows cross-platform analysis of input recordings without an
    emulator.
